{
  "prompt": "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two portions of garlicky tempeh and couscous skillet served in two round, simple, matte ceramic bowls. The camera is positioned at a 3/4 overhead angle (about 40°) to clearly show the textures within the bowls, with the primary bowl in focus and the second bowl softly blurred in the background. The couscous is fluffy and golden-brown from the broth, mixed with crumbles of seared golden-brown tempeh, vibrant dark green wilted baby spinach, deep red chopped sun-dried tomatoes, and tender quartered artichoke hearts. A delicate scattering of white crumbled feta cheese rests on top of the mixture. Soft natural side light from a window on the left highlights the glistening oil droplets and the varied textures of the ingredients. The bowls sit on a rustic, aged oak wooden table with visible grain and marks. Props include a wooden spoon resting on the surface next to the bowls and a few scattered crumbs of tempeh and a stray piece of spinach near the edge of the table. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating—lived-in, warm, and authentic. Includes slight natural imperfections like an asymmetric garnish placement and a stray speck of oregano. The color temperature is warm and inviting, characteristic of golden hour. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a photograph taken by a professional food photographer for a high-end cookbook."
}
